My current custom implementation of this is based in an example:

``` jsx
import React from 'react'
import {Range, RefinementList} from 'react-instantsearch'
import './style.scss'

function SidebarSection ({title, item}) {
  return (
    <article className='pa3 pa4-ns'>
      <div className='f6 fw6 ttu tracked pb2 bb b--black-10 black-70'>{title}</div>
      {item}
    </article>
  )
}

function Facets () {
  return (
    <div data-app='facets-wrapper'>
      <SidebarSection
        title='category'
        item={
          <RefinementList
            attributeName='category'
            id='c'
            operator='or'
            limitMin={10}
          />
        }
      />
```

But this not enough. The point is, when `{item}` render `null`, the wrap around the element is rendered. In this case the output is:

<img width="308" alt="screen shot 2016-10-16 at 01 08 09" src="https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/2096101/19413930/08a17366-933d-11e6-9f66-8f4e1cbf02b9.png">

This PR was a work around. I suppose that if you expose a mechanism to know if the item will be rendered for be possible associate a correct  wrapper to be rendered with the element will be a better solution.

maybe something like `itemWrapper`? I saw `itemComponent` for a other element in docs.

Hmm, I fixed the problem with the imports doing:

``` jsx
import React, {PropTypes, Component} from 'react';
import pick from 'lodash/pick';
import themeable from 'react-instantsearch/src/core/themeable';
import translatable from 'react-instantsearch/src/core/translatable';
import List from 'react-instantsearch/src/components/List';

const theme = {
  root:  {},
  item:  {},
  itemSelected:  {},
  itemLabel:  {},
  itemCount:  {},
  showMore:  {},
  showMoreDisabled:  {},
  itemLabelSelected:  {},
  itemCountSelected:  {},
  itemCheckbox: {},
  itemCheckboxSelected: {}
}
```

new problem:

```
warning.js:36 Warning: Failed prop type: Required prop `refine` was not specified in `RefinementList`.
```

Now I don't know what do 🎃

oh, I need to connect it!

``` jsx
const CustomRefinementList = themeable(theme)(
  translatable({
    showMore: extended => extended ? 'Show less' : 'Show more',
    count: count => count.toLocaleString(),
  })(RefinementListFactory)
);

export default RefinementList.connect(CustomRefinementList);
```

Looks horrible but it's something
